1
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,740
(Chen Hewen and Sha Yue'er's City Date)

2
00:00:08,760 --> 00:00:10,000
Is this something you like?

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,960
I am starving. It looks...

4
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:13,320
You have a good eye for food.

5
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:14,160
It looks like shrimp.

6
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,720
Okay.

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,960
You should have some too.

8
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:16,920
It smells wonderful.

9
00:00:18,680 --> 00:00:19,840
Let me see if I can

10
00:00:19,840 --> 00:00:20,400
get you one.

11
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,320
Thank you.

12
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:23,640
Do you usually skip dinner?

13
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,360
I eat dinner.

14
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,180
(Looks)

15
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:30,640
Thank you.

16
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,320
This spoon hasn't been used.

17
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:33,880
It looks like fruit.

18
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:36,640
I think it is...

19
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:37,560
Salmon.

20
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,080
It looks like
it is a salmon feast tonight.

21
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,080
Are these chicken wings?

22
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:44,400
Possibly.

23
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,360
Didn't you already have one?

24
00:00:48,140 --> 00:00:49,660
(Laughs)
I forgot.

25
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:50,840
I had no idea what it was.

26
00:00:53,480 --> 00:00:55,200
How did you end up choosing this place?

27
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:56,480
Mainly because I wanted you

28
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:57,360
to get to know me better.

29
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:02,560
I hope you have a good time.

30
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:03,220
(Looks)

31
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:05,000
You are dressed rather formally today.

32
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:05,720
(Business attire)

33
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,000
Are the two of us here to discuss

34
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:07,600
(Joking)
a business deal?

35
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,000
What do you think, Mr. Chen?

36
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,840
Can we get our multi-billion-dollar

37
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:11,640
project finalized?

38
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:13,440
Have your lawyer

39
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:14,520
prepare the contract tomorrow.

40
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:21,760
What kind of relationship...

41
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:24,800
would you find

42
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:27,280
comfortable?

43
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:28,000
What kind of dynamic

44
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:29,520
would you prefer?

45
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,320
That question is rather broad.

46
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:34,640
Could you give me an example?

47
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:35,920
For instance, what kind of dynamic

48
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,560
would make you feel comfortable?

49
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,680
You could say that you would like

50
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:41,440
to have some personal space.

51
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:42,520
Then you might feel that absence

52
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,480
makes the heart grow fonder.

53
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:44,080
Something like this.

54
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:45,320
Would you prefer to have a certain...

55
00:01:45,800 --> 00:01:47,120
I actually enjoy spending

56
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:49,400
a lot of time together.

57
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,720
Staying home and reading together?

58
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,080
We can do anything together
as long as we are together.

59
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:54,720
So you prefer to see
each other every day?

60
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:55,920
Not necessarily every day.

61
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:57,120
Just frequently.

62
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:00,400
Spending time together

63
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:01,560
at home?

64
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:04,160
Or would you prefer
to do more activities together,

65
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,000
such as traveling?

66
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:05,440
Then...

67
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,080
Either is fine.

68
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:06,760
Either works for you?

69
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:10,440
But I think

70
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:12,160
traveling together would be fun.

71
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,480
There is somewhere I really want

72
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:14,080
to visit.

73
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:14,960
Where would you like to go?

74
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:16,280
Tibet.

75
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,600
I remember going there

76
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:18,760
with my grandmother as a child.

77
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:21,200
When you travel,

78
00:02:21,200 --> 00:02:22,440
what kind of places do you prefer?

79
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:24,920
After seeing enough cultural sites,

80
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:26,320
I would rather spend time in nature.

81
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,560
That is true.

82
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,400
I dislike crowded places too.

83
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,800
Even when I travel,

84
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,120
I tend to avoid crowded places.

85
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,400
I would probably prefer

86
00:02:33,400 --> 00:02:35,120
somewhere less crowded and peaceful.

87
00:02:35,680 --> 00:02:36,760
As someone from Beijing,

88
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,120
have you ever climbed the Great Wall?

89
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:39,240
I have.

90
00:02:39,880 --> 00:02:40,960
But I have never visited
the Forbidden City.

91
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:42,560
Never?

92
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:43,440
I have passed by it,

93
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:44,840
but I have never been inside.

94
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:46,120
Why not?

95
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:48,840
Did you always think
there would be another chance?

96
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:49,760
I do not know why,

97
00:02:49,760 --> 00:02:50,560
but after all this time...

98
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,120
I should make time to visit.

99
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:53,200
Yes.

100
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:55,560
Can only one person

101
00:02:55,560 --> 00:02:57,800
go on the City Date each week?

102
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:00,520
It should be limited
to one person per week.

103
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:02,560
You sure know how to get what you want.

104
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,560
That is why I have always

105
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:09,240
told you not to feel pressured.

106
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,040
Whatever you choose,

107
00:03:10,040 --> 00:03:10,760
if I were in your

108
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:11,680
shoes, I would see nothing

109
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:12,360
wrong with it.

110
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,520
Because

111
00:03:13,520 --> 00:03:14,560
if I were your age,

112
00:03:14,560 --> 00:03:16,560
I might not have handled

113
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,560
things

114
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:18,560
as maturely as you have.

115
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,600
I am simply being honest.

116
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:23,100
(Laughs)

117
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,960
I think you are a very mature person.

118
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:25,760
You have your own thoughts,

119
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:26,960
your own

120
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:27,960
logic,

121
00:03:27,960 --> 00:03:29,000
and your own

122
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:30,800
pace.

123
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,920
So I will respect your decisions.

124
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,160
Let's go.

125
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:42,840
Want to play?

126
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,760
We can play together.

127
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:44,320
Okay.

128
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:46,520
Okay.

129
00:03:47,160 --> 00:03:48,000
Go ahead and break.

130
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:50,220
(Misses the ball)

131
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,360
Wait.

132
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:52,880
Let's start over.

133
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:53,400
I told you,

134
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,400
nothing happened between us.

135
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,440
- Nothing happened.
- Okay.

136
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:56,080
- Nothing happened.
- That is right.

137
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:56,920
Let's start over.

138
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:03,760
Nice.

139
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:10,280
Nice.

140
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:11,160
That was cool.

141
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:12,680
That was cool.

142
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,160
Almost.

143
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:19,600
You look cool.

144
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:20,960
I feel like I cannot hit it.

145
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:21,800
Do not move.

146
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:22,840
I want to take a picture of you.

147
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:23,520
I feel like it's...

148
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:24,320
You look hot.

149
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:26,760
I am.

150
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:30,180
(Takes camera)

151
00:04:30,200 --> 00:04:31,280
Three.

152
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,080
Two.

153
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:32,560
One.

154
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,000
Looks good.

155
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:34,880
It looks pretty good.

156
00:04:38,320 --> 00:04:39,040
It moved.

157
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,320
You did hit it.

158
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,560
(Comforting)
It is okay.

159
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:45,200
I am laughing so hard.

160
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:50,960
It ran away.

161
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:51,440
Okay.

162
00:04:52,200 --> 00:04:52,920
This is so difficult.

163
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,160
I noticed that my beginner's luck

164
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:54,800
has run out.

165
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:55,720
Let's try again.

166
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,320
Come on.

167
00:05:01,880 --> 00:05:02,800
Hit the green one.

168
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,480
Nice.

169
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:09,280
You have already developed a strategy.

170
00:05:11,740 --> 00:05:13,020
(Goes off course)

171
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:23,340
(Assists)

172
00:05:24,040 --> 00:05:24,680
Thank you.

173
00:05:24,680 --> 00:05:26,080
Okay.

174
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,440
Let's take a break.

175
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,440
Let's go boating.

176
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,160
Sure.

177
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:35,120
Let's go.

178
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:36,640
Come on.

179
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:37,560
Come on.

180
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,960
Wait.

181
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,120
Why are we going in circles?

182
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:43,660
(Going around in circles)

183
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:45,080
Wait, we are supposed to go together.

184
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,600
We have pushed all the grass
out of the way.

185
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:49,360
How do we get out of here?

186
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,120
Come on.

187
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,040
I am going to turn.

188
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:54,640
You paddle this side,
I will paddle the other.

189
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:55,480
Okay.

190
00:05:55,480 --> 00:05:56,360
Three, two, one.

191
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,200
Come on. Three, two, one.

192
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,200
Let's go.

193
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:58,760
Okay.

194
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,160
Go.

195
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:00,560
Okay.

196
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,320
I am ready.

197
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,040
Let's paddle forward together.

198
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:05,360
We...

199
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,000
We have got some skills.

200
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,400
I think we are the fastest

201
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:14,360
at rowing, right?

202
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,240
Yes.

203
00:06:16,160 --> 00:06:18,400
I realized that we only need
to paddle on one side to move forward.

204
00:06:18,400 --> 00:06:19,680
We have already figured out the trick.

205
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,320
We can do that together.

206
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:21,760
Yes.

207
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,400
We paddle

208
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:23,520
in turns.

209
00:06:23,520 --> 00:06:24,920
Yes, you know what I mean.

210
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:25,440
Yes.

211
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:27,520
There is water here now.

212
00:06:30,800 --> 00:06:31,440
This is beautiful.

213
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:32,880
- It is already beautiful.
- Okay.

214
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,480
All right.

215
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,240
How about we take a picture?

216
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:36,920
Sure.

217
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:38,000
Now is a good time to take one.

218
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:38,680
Sure.

219
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:39,360
Okay.

220
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:40,560
From this angle.

221
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:41,280
Okay.

222
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,960
Stay still.

223
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:44,120
Let's try it like this.

224
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:44,880
Okay.

225
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:45,920
Three.

226
00:06:45,920 --> 00:06:46,800
Two.

227
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,360
One.

228
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:49,760
It looks really good.

229
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,000
The same angle.

230
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:52,720
Three.

231
00:06:52,720 --> 00:06:53,800
Two.

232
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:54,280
One.

233
00:06:57,400 --> 00:06:58,360
The boat is swaying.

234
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,200
We need to hold it steady,

235
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,800
or it will fall into the water.

236
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:05,680
One.

237
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:06,200
Two.

238
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:07,440
Three.

239
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:11,680
All right.

240
00:07:11,680 --> 00:07:13,440
We are getting ready to head back.

241
00:07:13,440 --> 00:07:14,160
Heading back. Okay.

242
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:14,960
Ready to head back.

243
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:21,720
Okay, let's go straight ahead now.

244
00:07:21,720 --> 00:07:23,200
Okay. Let's go.

245
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,440
You paddle this side,
I'll paddle on the other.

246
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,120
No problem.

247
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:31,760
We need to paddle

248
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:32,680
in opposite directions.

249
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:33,920
Yes. That is the fastest way.

250
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:39,920
Sure.

251
00:07:39,920 --> 00:07:41,440
No problem.

252
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:44,080
Okay.

253
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:44,600
I understand now.

254
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:46,440
If we paddle together,
we will go much faster.

255
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:51,540
(Speeds up)

256
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,080
That is a little too fast.

257
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:56,160
What is this?
Is this some kind of speedboat?

258
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,720
Are we riding a yacht or something?

259
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,240
Wait. We are tilting.

260
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:00,960
We are tilting.

261
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:02,120
A couple of corrective strokes.

262
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,480
We are going even faster.

263
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,440
We are the rowing champions.

264
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,240
Back we go.

265
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,440
Let's get back to shore.

266
00:08:11,160 --> 00:08:12,040
That was incredible.

267
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:12,970
Oh my goodness.

268
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,920
We really are quite clever.

269
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,000
Is this a boat?

270
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,040
This is a rocket, actually.

271
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:18,720
Seriously.

272
00:08:18,960 --> 00:08:19,720
Let's get ashore.

273
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:20,360
All right.

274
00:08:21,440 --> 00:08:22,200
This is for you.

275
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:23,960
Thank you.

276
00:08:24,120 --> 00:08:24,680
This is a...

277
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,360
What is this?

278
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:25,680
Another one.

279
00:08:25,680 --> 00:08:26,640
What is this one?

280
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:27,440
Take a guess.

281
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,040
This is...

282
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:29,280
This is a capybara.

283
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,600
You get me.

284
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:32,680
You guessed them correctly.

285
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,040
This is a capybara.

286
00:08:34,040 --> 00:08:34,760
A capybara.

287
00:08:34,760 --> 00:08:35,280
Yes.

288
00:08:35,280 --> 00:08:36,080
So you...

289
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:37,800
This one is me.

290
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,720
So you get one...

291
00:08:39,920 --> 00:08:41,680
You get one...

292
00:08:42,840 --> 00:08:43,640
This is so much fun.

293
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:45,160
It feels like a public confession.

294
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,200
Sorry.

295
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,960
I just happened to be passing by.

296
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,520
A capybara blind box.

297
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:55,120
Seriously.

298
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:56,840
I really was just passing by.

299
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:58,280
Everyone was just passing by.

300
00:08:59,420 --> 00:09:00,500
